# Group `berkas`: who may use the SFTP file server on .103.
#
# A separate group on purpose: reusing `ecanteen` would silently give every canteen account access to the office files.
#
# Sysadmins (arif, joko) are deliberately excluded: sshd has `Match Group berkas` with `ForceCommand internal-sftp`, which would take away their SSH shell.
#
# The four members all have `/usr/sbin/nologin` shells. `arif` (auditor) is here although SSH login is denied: he may fetch files but not log in to the machine.

dn: cn=berkas,ou=groups,dc=bsp,dc=id
objectClass: posixGroup
cn: berkas
gidNumber: 20005
description: Boleh memakai server berkas SFTP di .103 (sftp saja, tanpa shell)
memberUid: dewi
memberUid: bagas
memberUid: intan
memberUid: arif
